\f1\fs26 PAPER\'92s computer humpers could find anyone: an Airborne, by the show-off lifestyles they had, and a Cloudborne, by their flashing armpits at a security devices. Not that Emil Kalheri had personally flashed an entrance request at the dock of Sunny Contemplations Funeral Home.\
Agent Jones knew the reputation of the mortuary as a resource funnel for the teaching hospital on whose campus it adjoined. It paid relatively handsomely for fresh bodies, which attracted a steady conga line of ambulances operated by corrupt orderlies. The bearers of Emil\'92s body must have needed the extra money; the mortuary was in another security zone from both Emil\'92s home and Travis\'92s office\'97crossing the boundary was often more trouble than the worth, and would\'92ve involved arguing the price with customs officials.\
Agent Jones attended the mortuary early in the evening. Emil was laid on a table among scores in the main necropsy room. Around him, a field of activity thrived. Rows of pathologists spoke quietly and precisely into microphones hanging from above, while they hacked, sawed and sliced through bone, meat and sinew. They slopped organs and tissue samples into jars, under the gaze of trainee physicians who watched in both fascination and disgust, some barely keeping down their lunch. Some ghouls giggled.\
\'93I will see his effects,\'94 Agent Jones told the medical gown attending Emil. The gown nodded and took him to a room of big gulping cabinets. From one drawer, she retrieved a crumpled bag. Agent Jones took it to a table, cut it open and examined the contents. He recognised the midnight-blue suit, the new shoes and the novelty socks. He pat everything down, fossicked into the shoes and turned everything else inside out.\
\'93Are you sure this is everything?\'94 he asked the gown.\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94\
\'93The security stream please.\'94 Agent Jones studied the stream and found no evidence of the disc. It had never arrived. Next, he examined the record of Emil\'92s delivery. \'93The ambulance hacks have the disc,\'94 he said.\

